{"tool_name":"intarna","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"intarna","version":"3.4.1","home":"https://github.com/BackofenLab/IntaRNA","documentation":"https://backofenlab.github.io/IntaRNA","license":"MIT","summary":"Efficient RNA-RNA interaction prediction incorporating seeding and accessibility of interacting sites.","identifiers":["biotools:intarna","doi:10.1093/nar/gkx279","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btn544","doi:10.1093/nar/gky329"],"build":{"number":3,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":["make",null,null,"pkg-config","gnuconfig"],"host":["boost-cpp","zlib","viennarna >=2.4.14*,<3","doxygen","perl","libgomp","llvm-openmp"],"run":["boost-cpp","libgomp","llvm-openmp"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/BackofenLab/IntaRNA/releases/download/v3.4.1/intaRNA-3.4.1.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["IntaRNA -h","IntaRNA -t CCCCCCCCGGGGGGGGGGGGGG -q CCCCCCC"]},"recipe_maintainers":["martin-raden","BackofenLab"]},"biocontainers":{"name":"intarna","identifiers":["biotools:intarna","doi:10.1093/nar/gku359","doi:10.1093/nar/gkx279","doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btn544","doi:10.1093/nar/gky329"],"license":"MIT","summary":"Efficient RNA-RNA interaction prediction incorporating accessibility and seeding of interaction sites\\n\\nDuring the last few years, several new small regulatory RNAs (sRNAs) have been discovered in bacteria. Most of them act as post-transcriptional regulators by base pairing to a target mRNA, causing translational repression or activation, or mRNA degradation. Numerous sRNAs have already been identified, but the number of experimentally verified targets is considerably lower. Consequently, computational target prediction is in great demand. Many existing target prediction programs neglect the accessibility of target sites and the existence of a seed, while other approaches are either specialized to certain types of RNAs or too slow for genome-wide searches.\\n\\nIntaRNA, developed by Prof. Backofen's bioinformatics group at Freiburg University, is a general and fast approach to the prediction of RNA-RNA interactions incorporating both the accessibility of interacting sites as well as the existence of a user-definable seed interaction. We successfully applied IntaRNA to the prediction of bacterial sRNA targets and determined the exact locations of the interactions with a higher accuracy than competing programs.","home_url":"https://github.com/BackofenLab/IntaRNA","keywords":["Base Sequence","Internet","Nucleic Acid Conformation","RNA","Sequence Alignment","Sequence Analysis, RNA","Structure-Activity Relationship","Sequence analysis","Transcriptome"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":2},"biotools":{"id":"intarna","home":"http://rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/IntaRNA/","summary":"sRNA target prediction.","addition_date":"2016-01-20T15:06:12Z","last_update_date":"2019-01-10T05:30:38Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"version":["1.2.5"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:intarna","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"rna@rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de","name":"Rolf Backofen","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8231-3323","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"wrightp@informatik.uni-freiburg.de","name":"Patrick Wright","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Patrick Wright","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"University Freiburg","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"rnateam","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/Help.jsp"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"RNA sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3495"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"note":"Prediction of interactions between two RNA molecules. Predicts target sites on mRNA for given non-coding RNAs (ncRNAs) like eukaryotic microRNAs (miRNAs) or bacterial small RNAs (sRNAs), but it can also be used to predict other types of RNA-RNA interactions","operation":[{"term":"RNA secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0278"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Feature table","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1270"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"},{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"}]},{"data":{"term":"Feature table","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1270"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Feature table","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1270"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]},{"data":{"term":"Image","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2968"},"format":[{"term":"EPS","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3466"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"}]},{"data":{"term":"Image","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2968"},"format":[{"term":"EPS","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3466"},{"term":"Image format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3547"},{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"IntaRNA - RNA-RNA interaction","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"rnateam","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gku359","metadata":{"abstract":"CopraRNA (Comparative prediction algorithm for small RNA targets) is the most recent asset to the Freiburg RNA Tools webserver. It incorporates and extends the functionality of the existing tool IntaRNA (Interacting RNAs) in order to predict targets, interaction domains and consequently the regulatory networks of bacterial small RNA molecules. The CopraRNA prediction results are accompanied by extensive postprocessing methods such as functional enrichment analysis and visualization of interacting regions. Here, we introduce the functionality of the CopraRNA and IntaRNA webservers and give detailed explanations on their postprocessing functionalities. Both tools are freely accessible at http://rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de. \u00a9 2014 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Backofen R."},{"name":"Georg J."},{"name":"Hess W.R."},{"name":"Kleinkauf R."},{"name":"Lott S."},{"name":"Mann M."},{"name":"Richter A.S."},{"name":"Sorescu D.A."},{"name":"Wright P.R."}],"citationCount":189,"date":"2014-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"CopraRNA and IntaRNA: Predicting small RNA targets, networks and interaction domains"},"pmcid":"PMC4086077","pmid":"24838564","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"IntaRNA - RNA-RNA interaction","home":"https://bio.tools/intarna","version":"1.2.5","summary":"sRNA target prediction.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:intarna:1.2.5/web/rna.informatik.uni-freiburg.de","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true,"help":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":214,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":7,"year":"2015"},{"count":10,"year":"2023"},{"count":11,"year":"2026"},{"count":13,"year":"2020"},{"count":17,"year":"2021"},{"count":17,"year":"2024"},{"count":18,"year":"2019"},{"count":18,"year":"2022"},{"count":22,"year":"2025"},{"count":23,"year":"2016"},{"count":25,"year":"2017"},{"count":31,"year":"2018"}],"doi":"10.1093/nar/gku359","pmcid":"PMC4086077","pmid":"24838564","ref_count":34,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1990"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2014"},{"count":2,"year":"2006"},{"count":4,"year":"2010"},{"count":4,"year":"2013"},{"count":5,"year":"20